# Vydon Commit Rules

See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for the contributor entry point.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

- `type` (required): `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `style`, `revert`.
- `scope` (optional, lowercase): `backend`, `worker`, `frontend`, `cli`, `sdk`, `charts`, `terraform`, `docs`, `ci`, or a package name.
- `subject`: imperative present (`add`, not `adds`/`added`), lowercase first letter, no trailing period, ≤ 72 characters.
- `body` (optional): explains **why**, not what. Wrapped at 72 columns.
- `footer` (optional): `Refs: VYD-201`, `Closes: #123`, or `BREAKING CHANGE: ...`.

## Atomicity

- One intent per commit. If the subject contains "and", split it.
- Refactor first, feature second. Never bundle.
- Formatting and lint auto-fixes go into a separate `style:` commit.

## Banned

- Emojis of any kind.
- Automated authorship trailers (`Co-Authored-By:` with `bot`, `noreply`, or `@users.noreply.github.com`), `Generated with ...`, `🤖`. The local `commit-msg` hook rejects them.
- Phrases like "This commit introduces", "Adds the ability to", "Implements a robust solution".
- `WIP`, `fix typo`, `misc`, `update`, `final`.
- Bullet lists in the subject line.

## Examples

Good:

```
feat(sqlmanager): support deferrable constraints on upsert

Postgres on-conflict updates were dropping rows when the target had
deferrable constraints. Defer the checks until commit so all conflicts
resolve in a single pass.

Refs: VYD-209
```

```
refactor(backend): replace interface{} with any
```

Bad:

```
✨ Added a new feature for handling deferrable constraints
```

```
fix stuff
```
